From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: backend: palette layers and the colour key (suniv)

Two backend features sun4i-drm never used (F1C200s User Manual 5.3.5):

- Palette layers: a layer in palette mode (ATTCTL0 bits 23:22 = 01)
  takes 1, 2, 4 or 8 bits per pixel as indexes into a 256-entry ARGB
  palette RAM. Offer DRM_FORMAT_C1/C2/C4/C8 where the RAM is known
  (suniv: 0x1000), with the pixel order DRM uses (ATTCTL1 PS = 01 for
  1/2/4 bpp), and a PALETTE plane property: a blob of up to 256 ARGB8888
  words. One RAM serves all layers, so two palette layers must carry the
  same palette.
- The colour key (CK_MAX 0x880, CK_MIN 0x884, CK_CFG 0x888, ATTCTL0 bits
  19:18): a COLOR_KEY plane property, bit 63 on, bit 62 match outside the
  range, bits 23:0 and 55:32 the lowest and highest RGB888 colour. One
  key for all layers, so one keyed layer at a time.

Also drop ARGB4444 and RGBA4444 on suniv: its manual has formats 12 and
13 reserved.
---
